 =?UTF-8?q?for=20ten=20years?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- Change the default session lifetime from 30 days to 3650 days so newly issued direct-pairing sessions last ten years on this private, single-operator deployment.
- Give renewable pairing-link sessions (a plain pairing link exchanged with a DPoP proof) the same 3650-day renewal window instead of 30 days: each renewal still returns a one-hour DPoP-bound access token and now moves the session's expiry ten years out, so a paired device left unused for more than 30 days stays signed in. A session issued with the 30-day window keeps that expiry until its next renewal, which moves it ten years out; one already past its 30 days has to pair again.
- Preserve explicit lifetime overrides and device revocation through Settings > Connections; existing expired sessions still require pairing again.
- Guard the default 3650-day issued-session lifetime in the existing active-session listing test, and the ten-year renewal window in the pairing-link DPoP renewal test.
- The remote access guide describes the ten-year window.

Integration details:
- Preserve upstream DPoP renewal-chain behavior, the one-hour renewable access token, the DPoP binding, the rule that only plain pairing links renew, the 30-day MCP client session TTL and every other explicit TTL; only the default session lifetime and the renewal window of pairing-link sessions change. RENEWABLE_SESSION_WINDOW reuses SessionStore's DEFAULT_SESSION_TTL (now exported), so both lifetimes are one constant.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. On 965ddc1d6c SessionStore.ts still declares DEFAULT_SESSION_TTL = Duration.days(30) and issues with input?.ttl ?? DEFAULT_SESSION_TTL (SessionStore.ts:653); the separate 30-day MCP client session TTL is untouched.

Port to b6ac2449f1: upstream dd512d86c5 (#37980) and e396bb2e26 (#37990) make direct pairing links send a DPoP proof and give such sessions a one-hour access token with a 30-day sliding renewal window (RENEWABLE_SESSION_WINDOW in EnvironmentAuth.ts, used by exchangeBootstrapCredentialForAccessToken and renewAccessToken), so a device idle for 30 days would have had to pair again. RENEWABLE_SESSION_WINDOW is now DEFAULT_SESSION_TTL. SessionStore keeps the window only as the session row's expires_at (issue writes issuedAt + renewalWindow, each renew writes now + renewalWindow through AuthSessions.extend, which refuses an expired or revoked row; the token carries only the rnw flag), so rows issued with 30 days move to ten years at their next successful renewal. EnvironmentAuth.test.ts: upstream's renewal case expects ten-year expiries, renews after 400 idle days and checks that a device idle for 3651 days pairs again (it fails with the 30-day window).

Port to d63b9c4c76: upstream 780db269df (#41330) replaced docs/internals/environment-auth.md with docs/internals/04_environment-auth.md, which no longer states the renewal window, so the environment-auth hunk is dropped; code unchanged.

